        "original_id": "d12d6277-214d-56a5-89cf-c075ecaea9b4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Menindee Lakes, Menindee, New South Wales, Australia, Menindee County, Darling River, Darling Harbour, Sydney\n- People: Ralph Darling\n- Organizations: Central Darling Shire\n\nFacts:\n- Menindee is a small town in the far west of New South Wales, Australia, in Central Darling Shire on the banks of the Darling River.\n- Menindee is frequently but erroneously spelled \"Menindie\".\n- Menindee had a sign-posted population of 980 and a 2011 census population of 449.\n- The Menindee Lakes lie in the far west region of New South Wales, Australia, near the town of Menindee.\n- The Menindee Lakes are located in Menindee County.\n- Ralph Darling is the namesake of local geographical features including the Darling River and Darling Harbour in Sydney.",
